docs.capability:
- declared by a manifest;
- has a typed request/response;
- binding is fixed by a snapshot/provider ID;
- receives minimal permissions;
- cannot change legal program state;
- logs provenance.

docs.court:
- `vocabulary` — the vocabulary id; `court` — the court's name; `decided` — the decision date (mandatory: without it a holding has no window of effect, §276.6);
- `plaintiff`, `defendant` — factor sets X_π, X_δ found by the court, subsets of the vocabulary lists;
- `outcome` — a polarity literal: favors π at positive polarity, δ at negative.

