docs.no_evidence:
- `P` is derived without direct evidence;
- evidence for `P` exists but is inadmissible;
- evidence is absent, but `P` was established by binding adjudication.

docs.not_known:
`not_known(P)`:

- does not derive `not P`;
- is only permitted in rule bodies;
- is a non-monotonic/status-sensitive dependency;
- requires stratification;
- must not be used as a substitute for an explicit closed-world declaration.

